#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:142
msgid "Example: `nixpkgs#hello`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:144
msgid ""
"These have the form _flakeref_\\[`#`_attrpath_\\], where _flakeref_ is a "
"[flake reference](./nix3-flake.md#flake-references) and _attrpath_ is an "
"optional attribute path. For more information on flakes, see [the `nix "
"flake` manual page](./nix3-flake.md).  Flake references are most commonly a "
"flake identifier in the flake registry (e.g. `nixpkgs`), or a raw path (e.g. "
"`/path/to/my-flake` or `.` or `../foo`), or a full URL (e.g. `github:nixos/"
"nixpkgs` or `path:.`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:152
msgid ""
"When the flake reference is a raw path (a path without any URL scheme), it "
"is interpreted as a `path:` or `git+file:` url in the following way:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:156
msgid ""
"If the path is within a Git repository, then the url will be of the form "
"`git+file://[GIT_REPO_ROOT]?dir=[RELATIVE_FLAKE_DIR_PATH]` where "
"`GIT_REPO_ROOT` is the path to the root of the git repository, and "
"`RELATIVE_FLAKE_DIR_PATH` is the path (relative to the directory root) of "
"the closest parent of the given path that contains a `flake.nix` within the "
"git repository. If no such directory exists, then Nix will error-out."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:164
msgid ""
"Note that the search will only include files indexed by git. In particular, "
"files which are matched by `.gitignore` or have never been `git add`\\-ed "
"will not be available in the flake. If this is undesirable, specify `path:"
"<directory>` explicitly;"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:168
msgid ""
"For example, if `/foo/bar` is a git repository with the following structure:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:178
msgid "Then `/foo/bar/baz/blah` will resolve to `git+file:///foo/bar?dir=baz`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:180
msgid ""
"If the supplied path is not a git repository, then the url will have the "
"form `path:FLAKE_DIR_PATH` where `FLAKE_DIR_PATH` is the closest parent of "
"the supplied path that contains a `flake.nix` file (within the same file-"
"system). If no such directory exists, then Nix will error-out."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:185
msgid ""
"For example, if `/foo/bar/flake.nix` exists, then `/foo/bar/baz/` will "
"resolve to `path:/foo/bar`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:188
msgid ""
"If _attrpath_ is omitted, Nix tries some default values; for most "
"subcommands, the default is `packages.`_system_`.default` (e.g. `packages."
"x86_64-linux.default`), but some subcommands have other defaults. If "
"_attrpath_ _is_ specified, _attrpath_ is interpreted as relative to one or "
"more prefixes; for most subcommands, these are `packages.`_system_, "
"`legacyPackages.*system*` and the empty prefix. Thus, on `x86_64-linux` `nix "
"build nixpkgs#hello` will try to build the attributes `packages.x86_64-linux."
"hello`, `legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.hello` and `hello`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:199
msgid ""
"If _attrpath_ begins with `.` then no prefixes or defaults are attempted. "
"This allows the form _flakeref_\\[`#.`_attrpath_\\], such as `github:NixOS/"
"nixpkgs#.lib.fakeSha256` to avoid a search of `packages.*system*.lib."
"fakeSha256`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:201
msgid "Store path"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:203
msgid "Example: `/nix/store/10l19qifk7hjjq47px8m2prqk1gv4isy-hello-2.10`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:205
msgid ""
"These are paths inside the Nix store, or symlinks that resolve to a path in "
"the Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:207
msgid ""
"A [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation) is also "
"addressed by store path."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:209
msgid "Example: `/nix/store/p7gp6lxdg32h4ka1q398wd9r2zkbbz2v-hello-2.10.drv`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:211
msgid ""
"If you want to refer to an output path of that store derivation, add the "
"output name preceded by a caret (`^`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:213
msgid ""
"Example: `/nix/store/p7gp6lxdg32h4ka1q398wd9r2zkbbz2v-hello-2.10.drv^out`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:215
msgid "All outputs can be referred to at once with the special syntax `^*`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:217
msgid "Example: `/nix/store/p7gp6lxdg32h4ka1q398wd9r2zkbbz2v-hello-2.10.drv^*`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:219
msgid "Nix file"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:221
msgid "Example: `--file /path/to/nixpkgs hello`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:223
msgid ""
"When the option `-f` / `--file` _path_ \\[_attrpath_...\\] is given, "
"installables are interpreted as the value of the expression in the Nix file "
"at _path_. If attribute paths are provided, commands will operate on the "
"corresponding values accessible at these paths. The Nix expression in that "
"file, or any selected attribute, must evaluate to a derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:227
msgid "Nix expression"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:229
msgid "Example: `--expr 'import <nixpkgs> {}' hello`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:231
msgid ""
"When the option `--expr` _expression_ \\[_attrpath_...\\] is given, "
"installables are interpreted as the value of the of the Nix expression. If "
"attribute paths are provided, commands will operate on the corresponding "
"values accessible at these paths. The Nix expression, or any selected "
"attribute, must evaluate to a derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:235
msgid ""
"You may need to specify `--impure` if the expression references impure "
"inputs (such as `<nixpkgs>`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:237
msgid "Derivation output selection"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:239
msgid ""
"Derivations can have multiple outputs, each corresponding to a different "
"store path. For instance, a package can have a `bin` output that contains "
"programs, and a `dev` output that provides development artifacts like C/C++ "
"header files. The outputs on which `nix` commands operate are determined as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:245
msgid ""
"You can explicitly specify the desired outputs using the syntax "
"_installable_`^`_output1_`,`_..._`,`_outputN_ — that is, a caret followed "
"immediately by a comma-separated list of derivation outputs to select. For "
"installables specified as [Flake output attributes](#flake-output-attribute) "
"or [Store paths](#store-path), the output is specified in the same argument:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:248
msgid ""
"For example, you can obtain the `dev` and `static` outputs of the `glibc` "
"package:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:256 source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:289
msgid ""
"and likewise, using a store path to a \"drv\" file to specify the derivation:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:263
msgid ""
"For `--expr` and `-f`/`--file`, the derivation output is specified as part "
"of the attribute path:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:270
msgid "This syntax is the same even if the actual attribute path is empty:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:276
msgid ""
"You can also specify that _all_ outputs should be used using the syntax "
"_installable_`^*`. For example, the following shows the size of all outputs "
"of the `glibc` package in the binary cache:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:280
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix path-info --closure-size --eval-store auto --store https://cache.nixos."
"org 'nixpkgs#glibc^*'\n"
"/nix/store/i2fn2mjgihz960bwa7ldab5ra5fhxznh-glibc-2.33-123                 "
"33208200\n"
"/nix/store/n2wnn3i47w6dbylh64hdjzgd5rrprdn8-glibc-2.33-123-bin             "
"36142896\n"
"/nix/store/v7dyz518sbkzl8x2a1sgk1lwsfd3d6gm-glibc-2.33-123-debug          "
"155787312\n"
"/nix/store/z4hv6ybyinqw9a3dwyl5k66a91aggylj-glibc-2.33-123-static          "
"42488328\n"
"/nix/store/lrjirf0j1rjnvif6amyp9pfcqr2km385-glibc-2.33-123-dev             "
"44200560\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:295
msgid ""
"If you didn't specify the desired outputs, but the derivation has an "
"attribute `meta.outputsToInstall`, Nix will use those outputs. For example, "
"since the package `nixpkgs#libxml2` has this attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:299
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix eval 'nixpkgs#libxml2.meta.outputsToInstall'\n"
"[ \"bin\" \"man\" ]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:304
msgid ""
"a command like `nix shell nixpkgs#libxml2` will provide only those two "
"outputs by default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:307
msgid ""
"Note that a [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation) "
"(given by its `.drv` file store path) doesn't have any attributes like "
"`meta`, and thus this case doesn't apply to it."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:312
msgid "Otherwise, Nix will use all outputs of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:314
msgid "Nix stores"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md:316
msgid ""
"Most `nix` subcommands operate on a _Nix store_. The various store types are "
